- (a) Categories; fees. The alcoholic beverage licenses which may be issued under this Ordinance are provided below. A schedule of annual fees for such licenses is set by the Council of the Town of Pine Mountain and maintained in the office of the Council of the Town of Pine Mountain. Each alcoholic beverage license bears a sole and separate license fee. The schedule for current fees will be changed from time to time upon adoption of a resolution by the Council of the Town of Pine Mountain at a regularly called meeting.

- (1) Wholesale liquor;

- (2) Wholesale malt beverage and wine;

- (3) Retail off-premises liquor:

- (4) Retail off-premises malt beverage and wine; (5) Retail on-premises malt beverage and wine;

- (6) Retail on-premises distilled spirits by the drink (available only to Licensees who have acquired a retail on-premises license for malt beverages and wine).

- (b) Purchase of license. The applicant for an alcoholic beverage license shall pay to the office of the Council of the Town of Pine Mountain, at the time the license is applied for, the annual license fee for operation for one year, or any part of the year, beginning on the first day of January each year, and ending the thirty-first day of December each year. There shall be no proration of a license fee for a part of a year. The suspension or revocation of any license shall not entitle the licensee to a return of any portion of the license fee.
